<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Thank you for contacting Qantas Customer Care about your disrupted journey from {{{Case.Departure_City__c}}} on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<strong>Things don’t always go to plan</strong><br />
<br />
We’re committed to getting you to your destination on time, however, bad weather, natural disasters, technical problems and other issues can cause flight delays and cancellations, and your safety is our first priority.<br />
<br />
Though this cancellation was out of our control, I can understand how frustrating it must have been.<br />
<br />
We will always try to find you an alternative flight to get you to your destination, but if the options available are unsuitable and you no longer wish to travel, we are happy to provide a full refund.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If QF issued ticket add:-&nbsp;</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Your refund is on its way</strong><br />
<br />
I’ve checked with our ticketing department and can confirm a refund of ${{{Case.Recovery_Value__c}}} has now been processed back to the original form of payment.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If agent/other airline ticket add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
As your ticket was issued by -a travel agent/Expedia/American Airlines/etc-, rather than Qantas directly, they will need to process your refund.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If minimal refund due through fare or second instance add:-&nbsp;</strong></em><br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If a Frequent Flyer:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a gesture of goodwill, I’ve credited {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to your Frequent Flyer account.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If not a Frequent Flyer:-&nbsp;</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a gesture of goodwill, I’d like to arrange a credit of {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to you.<br />
<br />
Please can you let me know your Frequent Flyer number by replying to this email so I can credit points to your account. If you’re not already a member you can use this&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/frequent-flyer/join/code/familyfree">link</a>&nbsp;to join free of charge.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If requesting compensation add:-</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>We’re here to help</strong><br />
<br />
I was sorry to hear that the delay meant you missed your &lt;meeting/dinner/concert/planned accommodation/train&gt;.<br />
<br />
While we can’t provide compensation on this occasion, if you had any unexpected expenses because of the &lt;delay/cancellation&gt;, your travel insurance policy may cover these sorts of situations.<br />
<br />
Please let us know if you’d like us to provide you with an insurance letter to assist with any claim.<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
<br />
I want to assure you that I've passed your comments on to the relevant team for review.<br />
<br />
Thank you for taking the time to let us know about your experience and we look forward to welcoming you onboard again soon.</body>
</html>